            "review_title": "Review at Thanh pho moi binh duong",
            "review_text": "Timo S\nMunich, Germany11 contributions\n0\nHave some great pho at a 'historic place'\nMay 2018 • Couples\nThe food was really tasty. Basically they serve two dishes: pho with chicken and pho with beef. Chilies, kaffir limes, fried bread sticks and a big basket of herbs on the side to spice up your meal. \n\nAt first sight the restaurant looks like any other pho establishments in Vietnam. But it has an interesting history. During the American War this was a meeting place for high ranking Vietcong who planned the Saigon part of the Tet offensive here. The place is still run by the same family that ran it back then. Framed pictures remind the visitor of the place's history. We read that there is a private museum with more pictures upstairs but the owner wasn't interested to take us there. Anyway the soup alone makes this place worth a visit.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten May 9, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
