            "review_text": "canebrook\nNew York City, New York64 contributions\n0\nCome here for the history as well as the food\nMar 2018 • Business\nPho Binh is a modest place, though the food is very good. But the real attraction is that the restaurant served as a secret Viet Cong center during the American War, and the upstairs room has a small but very interesting collection of photographs and memorabilia from that time. Recommended and unusual.\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 21, 2018",
