            "review_text": "Ken L\n22 contributions\n0\nGreat pho and a cool slice of history to go with it.\nDec 2016 • Couples\nThe food was good quality and a generous portion, we were given a laminated page when we sat down with an article on the owner who sadly passed away in 2006. A man who later turned out to be the cleaner then approached us and said he'd be more than happy to show us around upstairs after we ate. We finished our tasty msg free (see below) soup.\n\nThe room upstairs was a tribute to the Viet Cong who planned their attack on the US embassy there in secret in 1968. He gave us a passionate personal tour and explained who the people in the pictures were and their roles with great pride. He obliged in taking plenty of photos of my girlfriend and I and made us feel very welcome. \n\nIf you come to Ho Chi Minh and don't visit here you're missing out. \nA great little tour and good food all for the price of a bowl of pho. I've no idea why it's not busier.\nRead more\nWritten December 26, 2016",
