            "review_title": "Review at Thanh pho moi binh duong",
            "review_text": "Gavin W\n5 contributions\n0\nMSG Bomb!!!\nOct 2016 • Couples\nWe have lived in Saigon for a few years, but until today we had never made the trip up the road to Phở Bình’s. When we arrived, there were no other customers there but we sat down and ordered two bowls of phở tái (rare beef) for 50k dong each. \n\nThe little ambience that the simple restaurant might have had was destroyed by a blaring TV further back in the dining area which made it difficult to chat. We were presented with a typically enormous plate of rau (fresh green leaf vegetables and herbs).\n\nOur two bowls of phở looked good when they arrived and each had a generous amount of beef. The taste was reasonable, but far too salty (or so I thought), so we had to add lots of lime to balance the flavour.\n\nWe paid our bill and left, and then around 10 minute later the unmistakable symptoms hit us: increased heart rate, dizziness, tingling hot skin and pressure around the face and neck. We had consumed an MSG bomb!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 2, 2016",
