            "review_title": "Review at Thanh pho moi binh duong",
            "review_text": "Lynseyf\nNewport, United Kingdom64 contributions\n0\nA souper stop for lunch & a little piece of history\nMar 2016 • Couples\nWhilst this isn't a bustling pho shop, it is a little piece of history in Ho Chi Minh. After a decent bowl of pho (beef was the only option when we were there, but it was good) we were given articles about the history of the shop to read through, before being shown around the upstairs of the shop, which served as secret Viet Cong headquarters, by a man who had himself fought during the war. A fascinating place, full of history and surprisingly not full of tourists.\nRead more\nWritten March 29, 2016",
