            "review_title": "Review at Thanh pho moi binh duong",
            "review_text": "Travelling Kat\nSydney, Australia188 contributions\n0\nA war buff must\nJan 2016\nJust for the historical significance this restaurant is worth the visit. A very unassuming Pho shop. Pho is twice the price of most shops but at $60k vnd and the fact you can say you ate there, is worth it. The owner of the shop has passed away but the family keep the place going. Once you sit down they will give you a book that has articles about the owner and once you have finished they will take you upstairs and show you around the room that the Tet offensive was planned in. The furniture is the original as it was and the room has been set up as little shrine to the owner. Its a good idea to stop in here for a snappy lunch and cultural/historical experience.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 22, 2016",
