            "review_text": "brendanhoranhk\nHong Kong, China143 contributions\n0\nAmazing place in history, decent pho\nJan 2016 • Friends\nYou would not come to this place just for the Pho, not that the Pho is bad but its nothing special.\nWhat you do come here for is the upstairs room. The price of your Pho will be higher to cover the costs of keeping such a piece of history in shape. \n\nWe sat down, ordered our Pho and some drinks. One of the staff members then come over with a few photo albums and a lamented news paper clipping. Do take time to flick though the photo album. There are some interesting photo's in there. \nOnce we where done eating the Pho and looking at the photo albums the staff member asked us to follow him up a stair case and into a small room.\nThis room is lined with photos. The staff member than did his best to explain who was in the photo's and what they did. The photo's also had English descriptions under them.\nThe staff member talked to us about what happened and got some photo's of us. The room it self is well kept.\n\nIt was amazing to stand in a piece of history. This place is worth the trip out if your into history.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 9, 2016",
