            "review_title": "Review at Thanh pho moi binh duong",
            "review_text": "Ella N\n10 contributions\n0\nSneaky Good Noodles\nDec 2015 • Family\nThis was one of the coolest additions to our trip. The upstairs room in this small noodle shop is where the VC plotted out the Tet Offense in 1969, and it is a completely unknown historical gem. We sat down for noodles and were immediately recognized as tourists interested in the historical aspect of the place. The owner brought us some fascinating photo albums and gave us a tour of the upstairs 'museum' which was super cool. I highly recommend making this stop--it's a bit off the beaten path but it's worth it!\nRead more\nWritten December 23, 2015",
